      "content": "# Newly Launched AI Coding Tools (July 15-29, 2026)\n\nComprehensive research of AI coding tools launched in the 14 days before July 29, 2026.\n\n## 1. Full AI IDEs (similar to Cursor/Windsurf)\n\n### [KlaatCode](https://github.com/KlaatAI/klaatcode)\nOpen-source AI coding agent for the terminal. Claude Code-grade accuracy with smart model routing — uses the right AI model for each task, cutting costs 10x. Supports Claude, GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek & more.\n- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Terminal Agent\n\n### [BossConsole](https://github.com/risa-labs-inc/BossConsole)\nOpen-source, multi-platform harness for AI agents — a native, multi-threaded operator's console (JVM, not Electron) to run Claude Code, Codex, Gemini or OpenCode with a real browser, terminal, editor, secrets & 100+ MCP tools. Built for enterprises, science & research.\n- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Agent Harness\n\n### [Identra](https://github.com/identra-dev/identra)\nA desktop canvas for running coding agents.\n- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE\n\n### [CoDes](https://github.com/sorsama/CoDes)\nOpen-source desktop workspace for running coding-agent CLIs side by side.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Desktop Workspace\n\n### [nvim-agent-workbench](https://github.com/shanxierdan/nvim-agent-workbench)\nA project-aware Neovim IDE with persistent Codex sessions, tmux resume, and one-command setup.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Neovim Integration\n\n### [monoIDE](https://github.com/tripock/monoIDE)\nIt's an powerful IDE for notion AI agent that use Notion2API for route to notion chat.\n- **Launch Date:** July 26, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE\n\n### [EasyUseAIDE](https://github.com/john-ops-lab/EasyUseAIDE)\n面向个人开发者的跨 IDE Agent AI 编码工程化规则、Skills 与项目交付模板。Cross-IDE Agent AI coding engineering rules, Skills & project delivery templates for individual developers.\n- **Launch Date:** July 23, 2026\n- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Cross-Platform\n\n---\n\n## 2. AI Coding CLIs or Terminal Agents\n\n### [bbarit-agent-oss](https://github.com/bbarit/bbarit-agent-oss)\nOpen-source AI coding agent for your terminal — one Rust binary, 15+ LLM providers, 1,000+ models. A self-hostable Claude Code / Codex CLI alternative (MIT).\n- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n\n### [pi-dispatch](https://github.com/edgehero/pi-dispatch)\nRun the pi coding agent as a service — triggered on demand, on a cron schedule, or by a GitHub issue or pull request — in a container you control, with a durable queue, a spend cap, and a live admin panel.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Service\n\n### [infinitty](https://github.com/jasonkneen/infinitty)\nNative insanely fast terminal built for agents.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Terminal\n\n### [plank](https://github.com/aovestdipaperino/plank)\nInteractive terminal coding agent in Rust — runs the DeepSeek V4 Flash model locally on macOS (Metal), with a Ratatui TUI, a full tool suite, MCP, and persistent sessions.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n\n### [logan-cli](https://github.com/hoodini/logan-cli)\nLogan CLI - terminal AI coding agent by Yuval Avidani (YUV.AI). Fork of xAI Grok Build.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n\n### [GrokDesk](https://github.com/KAMIENDER/GrokDesk)\nGrok Build, beyond the terminal — native macOS workspace with full agent visibility, shared CLI sessions, and quota-aware multi-account routing.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/macOS Native\n\n### [Agent Manager](https://github.com/YoanWai/agent-manager)\nTerminal UI to manage AI coding-agent sessions (Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Grok Build) in tmux: live status, group tree, live pane preview, resource gauges.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Session Manager\n\n### [agent-console](https://github.com/buhuipao/agent-console)\nA local terminal control plane for Codex and Claude Code sessions—discover, monitor, resume, and work beside persistent workspace shells.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Control Plane\n\n### [Citizen-Agent](https://github.com/ElarineNycanis/Citizen-Agent)\n多模型开源 AI 终端助手，支持模型自由切换，集成视觉理解、AI 生图、音乐播放与 5 路并行子代理。An open-source AI terminal assistant with dynamic model switching, built-in vision understanding, AI image generation, music playback, and 5 parallel sub-agents.\n- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Multi-Model\n\n---\n\n## 3. Workflow-Specific AI Tools (debugging, refactoring, test generation)\n\n### [Kritt](https://github.com/Kritt-ai/open-kritt)\nOrchestrate AI agents to find real vulnerabilities in code.\n- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n- **Category:** Security/Code Analysis\n\n### [ponytail](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved)\nMakes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room. The best code is the code you never wrote.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Refactoring/Code Optimization\n\n### [code-humanizer](https://github.com/LeonardNJU/code-humanizer)\nhumanizer, but for code — an agent skill that removes AI-generated code slop: duplicated helpers, try-import fallbacks, broad excepts, speculative abstractions. Test-gated, behavior-preserving.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** Refactoring/Code Cleanup\n\n### [idea-refiner-skill](https://github.com/BURIBURI-ZAEMON1/idea-refiner-skill)\nRefine an early idea or creative concept into a coherent, evidence-aware design and durable Markdown master spec/PRD.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n- **Category:** Product Design/Planning\n\n### [idea-starter](https://github.com/ky-zo/idea-starter)\nBatteries-included, agent-guided starter for turning an idea into a deployed product.\n- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n- **Category:** Product Development Workflow\n\n### [idea-clarifier](https://github.com/guage1029/idea-clarifier)\n一个在写 PRD 前无情拷问产品想法、澄清需求价值与商业假设的 Agent Skill。An Agent Skill that ruthlessly questions product ideas before writing PRDs, clarifying demand value and business assumptions.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** Product Requirements\n\n### [Instruckt Laravel](https://github.com/sam-jamestty1474/instruckt-laravel-mcp-debug-tool)\nInstruckt Laravel v2026 is a Laravel/PHP package for live visual debugging of AI development flows, combining observability, MCP tooling, and AI-friendly feedback.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n- **Category:** Debugging/Observability\n\n### [Multi-LLM Debugging Bridge](https://github.com/HoziMurayama/Multi-LLM-Debugging-Bridge)\nAn MCP server that connects multiple OpenAI-compatible LLMs with shared tool access. Inspired by rubber duck debugging, it lets users discuss problems with different AI models, gather diverse insights, perform research, and compare responses.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Debugging/Multi-Model\n\n### [vibe-coding-toolkit](https://github.com/derek030208-design/vibe-coding-toolkit)\nCurated Claude Code skills for AI code quality control & creative writing.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** Code Quality/Workflow\n\n---\n\n## 4. AI Code Agents with Project/Workspace Memory\n\n### [MemTensor](https://github.com/MemTensor/memmy-agent)\nA personal AI agent & local memory hub for all AI agents like Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw and Hermes Agent. Gives every AI one shared, fully controlled memory and persistent context — all AI remember the same you.\n- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n- **Category:** Memory/Persistent Context\n\n### [cindy](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy)\nConsider it done. The open-source AI agent that works out of the box. 想到，就能做到。开源、开箱即用的 AI Agent。\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** General Purpose Agent/Project Memory\n\n### [openclaude-improved](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/openclaude-improved)\nruns anywhere. uses anything. A versatile Claude-based agent with broad model support.\n- **Launch Date:** July 26, 2026\n- **Category:** Multi-Model Agent\n\n### [pinvou-agent](https://github.com/Pinvou/pinvou-agent)\nOpen-source desktop AI agent for tools, files, knowledge, workflows, and real deliverables.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Desktop Agent/Knowledge Management\n\n### [goutoujunshi](https://github.com/powerycy/goutoujunshi)\n一个先接住情绪、再分析关系并给出可执行策略的 Codex 恋爱军师，内置心理、法律、社会、人文、哲学、婚姻家庭与性学知识库。A Codex relationship advisor that first addresses emotions, then analyzes relationships and provides actionable strategies.\n- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n- **Category:** Specialized Agent/Domain Knowledge\n\n---\n\n## 5. Open-Source AI Coding Agents\n\n### [Cindy](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy)\nConsider it done. The open-source AI agent that works out of the box. 想到，就能做到。开源、开箱即用的 AI Agent。\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Agent\n- **Homepage:** https://cindy.app\n\n### [KlaatCode](https://github.com/KlaatAI/klaatcode)\nOpen-source AI coding agent for the terminal. Claude Code-grade accuracy with smart model routing.\n- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source CLI Agent\n\n### [BossConsole](https://github.com/risa-labs-inc/BossConsole)\nOpen-source, multi-platform harness for AI agents.\n- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source IDE Harness\n\n### [bbarit-agent-oss](https://github.com/bbarit/bbarit-agent-oss)\nOpen-source AI coding agent for your terminal — one Rust binary, 15+ LLM providers, 1,000+ models. A self-hostable Claude Code / Codex CLI alternative (MIT).\n- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source CLI Agent\n\n### [CoDes](https://github.com/sorsama/CoDes)\nOpen-source desktop workspace for running coding-agent CLIs side by side.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Desktop Workspace\n\n### [approving](https://github.com/cocofhu/approving)\nApproving is an open-source, self-hostable platform for turning coding agents into visual, reviewable, and recoverable delivery workflows. Agents run in real Docker sandboxes, exchange structured artifacts, and pause for human Approve at critical nodes.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Workflow Platform\n\n### [autodev-studio](https://github.com/krishagarwal314/autodev-studio)\nAutonomous multi-agent SDLC harness: describe a feature in plain English and AI agents scope, code, test, review, and open a PR — grounded in a one-time knowledge base of your repo.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source SDLC Platform\n\n### [DarkPs-Agent-CLI](https://github.com/dark-ps/DarkPs-Agent-CLI)\nExtensible local-first AI agent framework for automation, coding, tools, and multi-model workflows.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Agent Framework\n\n### [argus](https://github.com/Elysium-Labs-EU/argus)\nDeterministic supervisor for multi-agent AI coding workflows: spawns workers, verifies diffs against git (not self-reports), and ships PRs. Written in Go.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Workflow Supervisor\n\n### [AutoAgent-VersionCode](https://github.com/jaydenqiu51/AutoAgent-VersionCode)\nAn AI Coding Agent Framework lets multiple AI agents work together on software projects. Specialized agents plan, write code, test, debug, review, and document code while sharing project context.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Open-Source Multi-Agent Framework\n\n---\n\n## 6. IDE-Integrated AI Tools\n\n### [cv4vs-agents](https://github.com/Corsinvest/cv4vs-agents)\nAgentic coding inside Visual Studio — Claude Code with a rich chat pane, an interactive terminal, and the IDE (editor, solution, debugger) exposed to the agent over MCP.\n- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n- **Category:** Visual Studio Integration\n\n### [nvim-agent-workbench](https://github.com/shanxierdan/nvim-agent-workbench)\nA project-aware Neovim IDE with persistent Codex sessions, tmux resume, and one-command setup.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** Neovim Integration\n\n### [Godot MCP Bridge](https://github.com/TomasLucasUTN/godot-mcp-bridge)\nMCP server for Godot 4 — give Claude, Cursor, or any MCP client full control of the Godot editor: 228 tools, live-tree editing with undo, DAP step debugger, GDScript LSP, runtime play-testing.\n- **Launch Date:** July 25, 2026\n- **Category:** Game Engine IDE Integration\n\n### [Agents Council](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/agents-council)\nMulti-agents collaboration plugin for Claude Code - orchestrate multiple AI agents (Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, etc.) for diverse perspectives.\n- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n- **Category:** Multi-Agent Orchestration Plugin\n\n---\n\n## 7. Workflow Orchestration Agents\n\n### [shipmates](https://github.com/saman-mb/shipmates)\nA crew of Claude Code sub-agents and slash-command workflows that drive a GitHub issue from open to a reviewed, CI-green pull request — autonomously. Flagship: /ship-issue.\n- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n- **Category:** GitHub Workflow Automation\n\n### [ECC](https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC)\nThe agent harness performance optimization system for Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor.\n- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n- **Category:** Performance Optimization\n\n### [agentic-awesome-skills](https://github.com/sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills)\nLocal, agent-first control plane with 1,987+ agentic skills, including CLI and MCP integration.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Skills Platform/Control Plane\n\n### [agentic-awesome-kits](https://github.com/KhaiTrang1995/agentic-awesome-kits)\nA universal collection of reusable Loop Engineering kits for AI coding agents—not just prompts. Each kit combines Skills, Rules, Templates, workflows, and validation loops.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** Workflow Templates/Kits\n\n### [agent-plugin-core](https://github.com/cs68614-hash/agent-plugin-core)\nCodex plugin foundation for native MCP App widgets, semantic tools, versioned state, automation skills, and verified agent workflows.\n- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n- **Category:** Plugin Foundation/Architecture\n\n### [kyn-agent-studio](https://github.com/cakbudak/kyn-agent-studio)\nBuild typed agent workflows and operate every run from authoritative evidence — OpenAI Build Week 2026.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n- **Category:** Workflow Studio\n\n### [real-agent-workflows](https://github.com/qianquandong/real-agent-workflows)\nThe AI workflows I actually run, open-sourced one at a time. Each one is a plain-markdown playbook — trigger, steps, output — not a plugin, and not locked to any tool.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n- **Category:** Workflow Playbooks\n\n### [symphlo](https://github.com/huisezhiyin/symphlo)\nLocal-first runtime for observable, debuggable AI-agent workflows with slidable autonomy and multi-agent/tool orchestration.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Workflow Runtime/Orchestration\n\n---\n\n## Additional Notable Tools\n\n### [hwatu](https://github.com/hongnoul/hwatu)\nFast, interruptible verification browser for AI coding agents: 35 ms checks, pixel diffs, live human hand-off.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n- **Category:** Verification/Testing\n\n### [cyvisguard](https://github.com/flankerhqd/cyvisguard)\nSecurity control plane for AI agents — identity and delegation, capability policy, data-flow taint and a live audit trail, enforced over MCP.\n- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n- **Category:** Security/Governance\n\n### [sigbound](https://github.com/surya-koritala/sigbound)\nRun AI coding agents in parallel on one git repo and safely auto-merge their work — only changes that build and pass tests land.\n- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n- **Category:** CI/CD Integration\n\n### [mentor](https://github.com/smixs/mentor)\nA session-insights skill for AI coding agents. Reads your local Claude Code and OpenAI Codex history and writes an /insights-style HTML report on how you work.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n- **Category:** Analytics/Insights\n\n### [pm-manager](https://github.com/wei63w/pm-manager)\nKnow what to fix next — local .pm governance skill pack for AI coding agents.\n- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n- **Category:** Project Management\n\n### [rtk](https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk)\nCLI proxy that reduces LLM token consumption by 60-90% on common dev commands.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Token Optimization\n\n### [codeburn](https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn)\nLocal tool tracking token usage and cost across 31 AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Cost Tracking\n\n### [awesome-ai-tokenomics](https://github.com/QuesmaOrg/awesome-ai-tokenomics)\nA map of what AI tokens actually cost, and where they're wasted vs. well spent.\n- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n- **Category:** Cost Optimization/Research\n\n### [ruvnet/ruflo](https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo)\nMulti-agent harness for deploying swarms, coordinating workflows, with adaptive memory and RAG integration.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Swarm Orchestration\n\n### [oraios/serena](https://github.com/oraios/serena)\nMCP toolkit providing semantic retrieval and editing capabilities, described as \"the IDE for your agent\".\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Agent IDE/Toolkit\n\n### [agno](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno)\nPlatform to \"build, run, and manage agent platforms\".\n- **Launch Date:** July 29, 2026\n- **Category:** Agent Platform\n\n### [tirth8205/code-review-graph](https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph)\nLocal-first code intelligence graph for MCP and CLI building persistent maps of codebases.\n- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n- **Category:** Code Analysis/Graph\n\n### [yvgude/lean-ctx](https://github.com/yvgude/lean-ctx)\nContext intelligence layer deciding \"what they read, remembers what they learn\" with 60-90% fewer tokens.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** Context Optimization\n\n### [metalbear-co/mirrord](https://github.com/metalbear-co/mirrord)\nRuns processes on local machines or AI agent environments as if in Kubernetes pods.\n- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n- **Category:** DevOps/Cloud Integration\n\n---\n\n## MCP Server Ecosystem (July 15-29, 2026)\n\n### [livetennisapi-mcp](https://github.com/livetennisapi/livetennisapi-mcp)\nMCP server for the Live Tennis API — give Claude, Cursor and other LLM agents real-time tennis scores, odds and model win-probability.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n\n### [Stormy Social Data API](https://github.com/OneInterface/stormy-cookbook)\nOpen-source cookbook for the Stormy Social Data API and MCP server — one REST API for TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), and Reddit.\n- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n\n### [App Store Connect MCP](https://github.com/erayendes/app-store-connect-mcp)\nHeimdall — MCP server for the Apple App Store Connect API & App Store Server API (StoreKit 2). 982 tools from Apple's official OpenAPI spec.\n- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n\n### [Godot MCP Go](https://github.com/regiellis/godot-mcp-go)\nControl a running Godot 4.7 editor and game directly from the terminal. Includes a Go CLI, editor addon, 312 commands, and an MCP server.\n- **Launch Date:** July 23, 2026\n\n### [symbolpeek-mcp](https://github.com/pioner92/symbolpeek-mcp)\nToken-efficient MCP server giving AI coding agents symbol-level reads of TS/JS, Rust, Python, Java, Go, JSON, and Markdown.\n- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n\n### [mcpgrade](https://github.com/TengByte/mcpgrade)\nLighthouse for MCP servers — score any MCP server on agent usability, not just spec compliance.\n- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Summary Statistics\n\n- **Total Tools Discovered:** 80+ AI coding tools\n- **Open-Source Projects:** ~90%\n- **Most Active Launch Dates:** July 15, 17, 18, 20-22, 24, 28-29\n- **Primary Categories:**\n  1. CLI/Terminal Agents (15+ tools)\n  2. Open-Source Agent Frameworks (12+ tools)\n  3. Workflow Orchestration (10+ tools)\n  4. IDE Integrations (8+ tools)\n  5. Memory/Context Tools (6+ tools)\n  6. Security/Governance (5+ tools)\n  7. MCP Servers (15+ tools)\n\n## Key Trends\n\n1. **Terminal-based AI agents** are exploding as a category\n2. **Multi-agent orchestration** is becoming mainstream\n3. **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** ecosystem is rapidly expanding\n4. **Cost optimization** tools (token tracking, smart routing) are emerging\n5. **Memory persistence** across agent sessions is a major focus\n6. **Security and governance** tooling is maturing\n7. **Workflow standardization** through templates and playbooks\n\n---\n\n**Research Date:** July 29, 2026\n**Time Period:** July 15-29, 2026 (14 days)\n**Sources:** GitHub API, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, Hacker News, DEV Community, Lobsters\n",
