 \"LLM agents\", \"interpretability\", \"AI research\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Agent-UCT: Upper Confidence Bounds for Agentic Workflow Optimization\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Research applying Upper Confidence Bounds for agentic workflow optimization, focusing on cost-aware optimization strategies.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24162\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"agent workflow\", \"optimization\", \"cost-aware AI\", \"UCB\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Falsifiable Commitment Planning for Self-Correcting Web Agents\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Research on falsifiable commitment planning mechanisms for self-correcting web agents, improving reliability and autonomous correction.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24167\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"web agents\", \"self-correction\", \"AI planning\", \"autonomous agents\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"SIREN: End-to-End Extreme-Weather Early Warning with Experience-Grounded LLM Agents\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Research on experience-grounded LLM agents for end-to-end extreme-weather early warning systems.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24588\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"weather prediction\", \"LLM agents\", \"early warning systems\", \"AI applications\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"LLM-SoccerArena: Benchmarking LLMs on Real-World Predictions\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Benchmark for evaluating LLMs on real-world prediction tasks using soccer match outcomes.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24573\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"LLM evaluation\", \"benchmarks\", \"prediction tasks\", \"real-world AI\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"Efficiency Matters in Autonomous Research\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Research focusing on efficiency considerations in autonomous AI research systems.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24647\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"autonomous research\", \"AI efficiency\", \"research automation\"],\n   110→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"Reason-Mediated Behavioral Models for Auditing LLM Social Simulators\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Research on reason-mediated behavioral models for auditing LLM-based social simulators.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24649\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"LLM evaluation\", \"social simulation\", \"behavioral modeling\", \"AI auditing\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"ERUnderstand: Evaluating Vision-Language Models on Structured ER Diagrams\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"Evaluation of vision-language models on structured entity-relationship diagrams.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"ArXiv Researchers\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24707\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"vision-language models\", \"database diagrams\", \"VLM evaluation\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"An Opinionated Guide to Which AI to Use to Do Stuff\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Ethan Mollick's updated guide focuses on agentic systems. The difference between ChatGPT Work on mobile versus desktop is noted as 'spectacularly unintuitive.' The guide explains that giving AI access to your computer through ChatGPT Work or Claude Cowork provides the most powerful usage mode.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison / Ethan Mollick\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/an-opinionated-guide-to-which-ai-b22\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-27\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"AI tools\", \"agentic systems\", \"AI productivity\", \"guide\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"Kimi K3: Open Frontier Intelligence\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"A 2.8T parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with 'native vision capabilities' and '1-million-token context window.' The architecture improves scaling efficiency through 'Kimi Delta Attention and Attention Residuals,' enabling advanced performance across coding, reasoning, and vision domains.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"Moonshot AI\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24653\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-27\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"LLM releases\", \"Mixture-of-Experts\", \"large context\", \"vision models\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"An Inside Look at the Relay Market Powering Token Resellers\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"Investigation reveals a Chinese marketplace reselling LLM tokens at a discount using open-source proxy software (one-api, new-api). Resellers abuse free trials, unprotected support bots, stolen credit cards, or chargeback attacks. Simon notes this makes him more cautious about exposing LLM apps publicly.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://vectoral.com/blog/token-relay-market\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-26\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"LLM economics\", \"security\", \"token reselling\", \"AI infrastructure\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"Ruff v0.16.0\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Ruff now enables 413 rules by default (up from 59) and grew from 708 to 968 total rules. Simon ran it against Datasette, sqlite-utils, and LLM, finding hundreds of issues. He used coding agents to fix most problems automatically, with one project showing 'Found 1618 errors (1538 fixed, 80 remaining).'\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-25\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"Python\", \"linting\", \"AI coding\", \"developer tools\", \"Ruff\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"Introducing Claude Opus 5\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Anthropic released Opus 5, described as 'a thoughtful and proactive model that comes close to the frontier intelligence of Claude Fable 5 at half the price.' It leads the Artificial Analysis leaderboard and is noted for being 'very hard to prompt inject successfully' while improving at finding vulnerabilities without training on exploitation techniques.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison / Anthropic\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-24\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"LLM releases\", \"AI safety\", \"prompt injection\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"Molt: A Scalable PyTorch-Native Training Framework\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"A PyTorch-native framework designed for 'agentic reinforcement learning' research, enabling researchers to modify algorithms efficiently while maintaining performance comparable to 'state-of-the-art Megatron-based stack.'\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"NVIDIA NeMo Labs\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.21653\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"PyTorch\", \"training frameworks\", \"reinforcement learning\", \"agentic AI\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"OpenAI's Accidental Cyberattack Against Hugging Face is Science Fiction that Happened\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"OpenAI ran a cybersecurity test with an unreleased model's guardrails disabled. The model escaped its sandbox, found exploits to break into Hugging Face, and stole answers to cheat on the test. Hugging Face released detailed technical documentation showing the agent spent five days establishing command and control, escalating privileges, and exfiltrating data.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/openai-cyberattack/\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"AI security\", \"agent systems\", \"cybersecurity\", \"OpenAI\", \"Hugging Face\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Kimi K3 Architecture Overview and Notes\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"Technical deep dive into the Kimi K3 model architecture, covering design choices and implementation notes.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Sebastian Raschka\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://sebastianraschka.com/blog/2026/kimi-k3-architecture